Detailed Explanation of DOM in JavaScript

1. What is the DOM?

The Document Object Model (DOM) is a programming interface for web documents. It represents the structure of a webpage so that programs can change the document structure, style, and content dynamically. JavaScript uses the DOM to interact with HTML and modify the page.

When a web page is loaded, the browser creates a DOM representation of the page, which can be manipulated using JavaScript.

