9. Traversing the DOM (Parent, Child, Sibling)

We can navigate between elements in the DOM using relationships.

(a) Accessing Parent Node

let child = document.getElementById("myChild");
console.log(child.parentNode);

(b) Accessing Child Nodes

let parent = document.getElementById("myParent");
console.log(parent.children); // Returns all child elements

(c) Accessing Sibling Nodes

let element = document.getElementById("myElement");
console.log(element.nextElementSibling);  // Next sibling
console.log(element.previousElementSibling);  // Previous sibling



