10. Performance Optimization in the DOM

Modifying the DOM frequently can slow down performance. Some best practices:
	1.	Minimize reflows and repaints – Avoid direct DOM modifications inside loops.
	2.	Use documentFragment – Improves performance when adding multiple elements.
	3.	Cache DOM elements – Store elements in variables instead of repeatedly querying them.
	4.	Use classList instead of style – Modify classes instead of applying inline styles.

Example using documentFragment:

let fragment = document.createDocumentFragment();
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    let newElement = document.createElement("p");
    newElement.innerText = `Item ${i + 1}`;
    fragment.appendChild(newElement);
}
document.body.appendChild(fragment);



